<?xml version="1.0"?>
<chroma>
<annotation>
lq3 CPU Chroma smoke test (1_build_chroma/lq/build_chroma_cpu.sh test).
From chroma's tests/chroma/hadron/propagator/unprec_clover_mg_proto.ini.xml (same action, source and
solver tolerances), changed toward a CPU production solve:
  - MG_PROTO_QPHIX_CLOVER_INVERTER: QPhiX AVX-512 on the fine level, mg_proto on the coarse levels;
  - NullVecs 24 32: mg_proto's QPhiX and coarse transfers dispatch only 6, 8, 16, ..., 64 colours
    (the shipped 12 aborts with "Unhandled dispatch size 12");
  - Blocking 4^4 then 2^4 on a 16^3 x 32 lattice, run on 2 ranks (-geom 1 1 1 2): local 16^4,
    coarse 4^4 and 2^4. A single rank cannot run mg_proto with QMP comms: with every direction on-node
    CommunicateHaloSyncInOMPParallel (mg_proto halo.h) calls QMP_start on a null handle;
  - no ERASE_MG_PROTO_*_SUBSPACE (cleanup only; it aborts when the subspace kind differs);
  - AntiPeriodicT true, matching the action's boundary 1 1 1 -1. The fermion state's links carry the
    antiperiodic sign; mg_proto's QPhiX operator wants unmodified links plus t_bc and stores links
    compressed (MG_QPHIX_COMPRESS12), rebuilding row 3 for det +1, so sign-flipped links come back
    wrong. With the shipped "false" the solve diverged (job 1364764).
</annotation>
